* Overall rules

  1. Metadata like `#+TITLE' and `#+AUTHOR' are concatenated (this is the same
     as if there were multiple metadata elements in the same file: i.e.
     inclusion has no effect).

  2. Relative paths specified in `#+INCLUDE:' directives are relative to the
     file they are contained in.

  1. Any OrgBody following an include is appended to the end of the last OrgBody
     in the included file.

  2. Any include following another include in the same OrgBody will start at the
     same level (even though the orgbody was relocated).

  3. Any first OrgBody block in an include is appended to the OrgBody where its
     include statement occurred.

  4. Any include in the first block occurs at level 0.

  5. minlevel is absolute for the file it includes, although the section nesting
     will return to the place it was when the include ends (although subsequent
     sections in the including file will be nested under the included file).

  6. Rule #3 still holds even with a minlevel specification.

  Third para of inc2.

